  "constraints": "* Input arrays/tensors are non-empty and well-formed\n* Floating point values are finite real numbers\n* Numerical operations must adhere to standard precision tolerances",
  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_handle_missing(records: list, fill_value: float = 0.0) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Handle Missing Values** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_handle_missing(records: list, fill_value: float = 0.0) -> dict:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n    return {'missing_counts': {c: int(df[c].isna().sum()) for c in df.columns}, 'imputed_records': df.fillna(fill_value).to_dict(orient='records')}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
